Verified with LemmaScript 0.6.9; Dafny 4.11.0.

sameRequest — ISSUE FOUND
JavaScript input rounding changes the result.

Formal input
  left        9007199254740992
  right       9007199254740993

JavaScript representation
  left        9007199254740992
  right       9007199254740992

Precision loss
  right       9007199254740993 → 9007199254740992

Result
  verified    false
  JavaScript  true

Cause
  JavaScript's IEEE-754 number representation rounds an exact formal numeric input before the function executes; distinct formal values can therefore collapse to the same runtime value.

Resolve
  Use an exact runtime representation, or restrict and enforce inputs to values that remain exact as JavaScript numbers.

